{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/authenticateDevice()"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authenticateDevice()"},{"type":"text","text":" — the mTLS device login (CONTRACT.md §6.1 rules 6-10)."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/authenticatedevice()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@discardableResult","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"authenticateDevice","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC","text":"AxiamClient","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/DeviceLoginResult","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC17DeviceLoginResultV","text":"DeviceLoginResult","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Issues ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/api\/v1\/auth\/device","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with no request body.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reachable only on a client configured with a client certificate"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (rule 7,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamConfig\/clientCertificate","type":"reference"},{"text":"). On any other client this refuses","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"CLIENT-SIDE with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamError\/auth(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"zero wire calls"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": without a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"certificate the server would answer ","type":"text"},{"code":"401","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" regardless, so going to the wire would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only turn a configuration mistake into an authentication failure.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On success the returned token is "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"adopted as this client’s credential","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a "},{"code":"login()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" result is (rule 6): every subsequent REST call this client sends —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"including every "},{"code":"management()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" operation — carries it as "},{"code":"Authorization: Bearer <token>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and withholds this client’s own cookie jar, so a session cookie from an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"earlier "},{"code":"login()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" can never ride alongside it. The server reads the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"axiam_access","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" cookie before "},{"code":"Authorization","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so keeping a stale one would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"silently run every later request as the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"previous"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" session’s principal, defeating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the point of authenticating fresh."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"There is no refresh token"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for this credential (rule 6, D-6 of the dogfooding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plan): the §9 single-flight guard has nothing to spend on it, so a later "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"401"},{"type":"text","text":" —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on this call, or on any request this client sends afterward — is surfaced as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no refresh attempt"}]},{"type":"text","text":". The caller recovers by calling"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authenticateDevice()"},{"type":"text","text":" again, which costs one TLS handshake."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every refusal is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"401"}]},{"text":" (rule 8, server T22.4): an unknown, untrusted,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"expired, revoked or unbound certificate, and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Server","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-type certificate, all map","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError"},{"text":". A ","type":"text"},{"code":"429","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from the route’s per-IP rate limiter maps to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/NetworkError"},{"text":" (§2), never ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AuthError"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"mapError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" already keeps the two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apart, so this method adds no special-casing for it, and it is never retried","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"here.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The token is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"certificate-bound"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cnf.x5t#S256"},{"type":"text","text":") when AXIAM itself terminated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the TLS handshake (rule 9); "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceLoginResult.tokenType"},{"type":"text","text":" stays "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"Bearer\""},{"type":"text","text":" either"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"way. A resource server verifying it locally MUST use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AxiamRequestAuthenticator.authenticateSenderConstrained(_:presentedThumbprint:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(or thread "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PresentedProofs"},{"type":"text","text":" through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authenticate(_:presentedProofs:)"},{"type":"text","text":") rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than the plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authenticate(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which — after this SDK’s own §10.1 rule 9 fix"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"— refuses a bound token with no evidence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","name":"Throws","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamError\/auth(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" client-side (no certificate configured, zero"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wire calls) or from the server’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"401"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamError\/network(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"429"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or any other non-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"200"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"authenticateDevice()","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"authenticateDevice","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AxiamClient","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"DeviceLoginResult","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC17DeviceLoginResultV"}],"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC18authenticateDeviceAC0E11LoginResultVyYaKF"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/AxiamClient/DeviceLoginResult":{"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/DeviceLoginResult","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DeviceLoginResult"}],"type":"topic","title":"AxiamClient.DeviceLoginResult","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/deviceloginresult","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"authenticateDevice()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" result (CONTRACT.md §6.1 rule 6).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DeviceLoginResult"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/do